 ["c8f5","Bf5","The Anti-Colle. Black solves his only structural problem before you can lock the door."],
 ["c2c4","c4!","Abandon the Colle. With the bishop outside the chain, e4 will never come with force; take the center instead."],
 ["c7c6","c6",""],
 ["d1b3","Qb3","Hitting b7, the pawn the bishop stopped defending when it left c8, while the c4 pawn leans on d5."],
 ["d8b6","Qb6",""],
 ["c4c5","c5","Gaining space and asking the queen a question."],
 ["b6c7","Qc7",""],
 ["f3e5","Ne5","The e5 outpost survives every version of this opening."],
 ["e7e6","e6",""],["f1d3","Bd3","Now the trade happens on White's terms."],
 ["b8d7","Nbd7",""],["f2f4","f4",""],
 ["f5d3","Bxd3",""],["b3d3","Qxd3","White has space, the e5 outpost and a plan; Black has traded his good bishop for a piece White was happy to give. This is the difference between reacting and following a recipe."]
